  "method": "I used only the three supplied files. I combined estimated cover fractions, false-color vegetation responses, grid descriptions, parcel geometry, canopy texture and shoreline patterns. I also retrieved comparable bank captions using TF-IDF cosine similarity; matches were weak and sometimes spectrally questionable, so they received little weight. NDVI judgments reflect approximate vegetation–water–bare-surface mixtures; directional comparisons use the spatial descriptions. CORINE labels are inferred from landscape structure, with uncertainty for forest subtypes and small features that may not receive separate labels. NDMI, NDBI and texture thresholds are qualitative predictions, not calculated measurements. For Q3, I followed the stated NDWI criterion, allowing possible positive responses from cloud, snow or deep shadow despite unconfirmed open water. Confidence is lower for obscured scenes, ambiguous classes and threshold-sensitive estimates. Q17 receives low confidence throughout because neither SWIR measurements nor the expected-value model is available."
